From a4d7bbaaa5dfff4a6cbeccb6ff40cfa45a1b9ff1 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Nicolas LE BAYON <nicolas.le.bayon@st.com>
Date: Wed, 8 Dec 2021 17:54:16 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 144/841] feat(st-ddr): construct firmware binaries

Create an unique FW binary per DDR type including dmem (offset=0) and
mem (offset=0x800) original binaries. Max binary size is then 0x8800.
Swap bytes to fit with platform needs. Keep original binaries.

These binaries are generated using dd commands (ddr3 example):
dd conv=swab bs=1 if=ddr3_pmu_train_dmem.bin of=ddr3_pmu_train.bin \
	seek=0
dd conv=swab bs=1 if=ddr3_pmu_train_imem.bin of=ddr3_pmu_train.bin \
	seek=$((0x800))

Upstream-Status: Inappropriate [ST downstream https://github.com/STMicroelectronics/arm-trusted-firmware.git 90035c1f14a55fae33e81cc3e334597dade40c34 feat(st-ddr): construct firmware binaries]
Change-Id: Ifd7d7c9d655b3a03cd55920536e43cb84055b48b
Signed-off-by: Nicolas LE BAYON <nicolas.le.bayon@st.com>
---
 .../st/ddr/phy/firmware/bin/ddr3_pmu_train.bin  | Bin 0 -> 21396 bytes
 .../st/ddr/phy/firmware/bin/ddr4_pmu_train.bin  | Bin 0 -> 29384 bytes
 .../ddr/phy/firmware/bin/lpddr4_pmu_train.bin   | Bin 0 -> 34412 bytes
 3 files changed, 0 insertions(+), 0 deletions(-)
 create mode 100644 drivers/st/ddr/phy/firmware/bin/ddr3_pmu_train.bin
 create mode 100644 drivers/st/ddr/phy/firmware/bin/ddr4_pmu_train.bin
 create mode 100644 drivers/st/ddr/phy/firmware/bin/lpddr4_pmu_train.bin

